<h1>About</h1>
<p>This site reports the TLS version your client used to reach it. TLS is the
protocol that encrypts traffic between your browser and a website — the padlock
in the address bar.</p>
<p>Newer versions are faster and harder to attack. Most browsers now negotiate
<code>TLS 1.3</code> or <code>TLS 1.2</code>; the older <code>TLS 1.0</code> and
<code>TLS 1.1</code> are deprecated and worth leaving behind.</p>
<p>The home page shows whatever version your browser and this server settled on
for that request. If you'd rather have it as data, fetch
<a href="/v1/version.json"><code>/v1/version.json</code></a>.</p>
<p><a href="/">← Check my version</a></p>
